d that her father planted in her that  if rhaenyra ascends to this Throne her  son's lives will be in danger and as  annoying as the adult version of Allison  is revealing herself to be this does  make the stakes clear at least from her  perspective in her mind people who are  jocking for power will question renera's  claim based on her son's appearances and  that will give her a reason to eliminate  the other possible heirs I.E Allison's  children in the time since we last Saw  Damon grabbing his niece's face at the  wedding Feast he's married Lena Valerian  and they had twins named Bella and Reina  we catch up with them in pentos where  you get to sense that they're  celebrities due to their dragons and  Damon's exploits in the stepstones  there's a fun scene with him and his  wife riding their dragons where we see  just how big Veigar is their daughters  also had cradle Lakes but only Bayless  hatched this means that they have three  dragons in their little family at the  moment and this is worth an offer of a  free mansion and lands from the prince  of pentos if they're willing to relocate  and make themselves a deterrent for the  triarchy the couple is split on this  Damon likes the idea of the simple  transaction of riches in exchange for  the presence of their dragons Lena wants  her children to be raised with their  family according to their Birthright and  would rather have a dragon Rider's end  instead of growing old and fat in the  middle of nowhere after raniera listens  in on Lionel strong complaining to his  son about how his indiscretions with her  matter for their family and how it puts  them at risk we see that while Leonor is  mostly content with their agreement that  leaves him free to hang around the  palace enjoying the Finer Things in life  while partying with his lovers he's  heard about fighting going on in the  stepstones and that has him wanting to  get back out there to spice things up  Rainier won't hear a bit since after  Joffrey's birth she realizes that the  rumors about their parentage are  swirling around their family and in the  end she pulls Rank and commands him as  his princess and heir to the Iron Throne  to remain at her side after Elena  explains to her daughter Reina that  she'll have to follow in her footsteps  and claim her Dragon just as she did  with vegar she goes to tell Damon about  raniera's new son he puts a finer point  on how Harwin being the father is  basically an Open Secret and there is  some interesting stuff going on here  that will be important down the road but  I can't help but feel like they  downplayed the time they spent with Lena  and Harwin based on how this episode  ends she seems to understand that him  not really being a present husband or a  good father has more to do with him and  his feelings about being exiled from his  family rather than her and she says  she's made peace with it at a small  council meeting after they discussed the  situation with the triarchy with her  back against the wall renera tries to  extend an olive branch to the Queen by  suggesting that they marry her Heir Jace  to her daughter Helena she's right in  thinking that this would solve all her  problems and viserys loves the idea but  even before they get interrupted by  rhaenyra's milk leaking and bleeding  through her dress it's clear that  Allison doesn't have any intention of  getting on board with her plan she makes  this plane to the king in the hall  afterward telling him he can follow  through with it when she's cold in her  grave Lionel follows that up by trying  to resign his post as hand of the king  and because he won't say out loud what  the shadow that hangs over his house is  viserys refuses to let him do that  Lionel has been portrayed as the one  person at court that gives the king good  advice regardless of how it might  benefit him personally and when Allison  has dinner with his son Laris they agree  that he's now compromised he can no  longer give unbiased counsel to the king  because his son and illegitimate  grandsons lives could be at stake there  is an interesting parallel baked into  this to when viserys does the exact same  thing with Otto who eventually does come  out with the truth the situation is  different because of the immediate  Stakes that are involved but we see  Allison run with this idea and use that  as a reason why her father should be  reinstated and it's a great touch when  Laris points out that he wouldn't be  impartial either and Allison yells out  no but he would be partial to me I  mentioned how Emma Darcy's opening  sequence really put her stamp on her  character and I think this is where it  happens with Olivia Cook's Allison and I  kind of love the contrast of her big  moment coming at the end of a slow boil  and what that says about the differences  between the characters from there things  ask escalate quickly Laris goes down to  the black cells and offers Mercy to  three criminals for the small price of  having their tongues cut out this felt  somewhat gratuitous I mean I suppose  he's doing this so they can't tell  anyone he's behind what they're about to  do but I also wonder if we're supposed  to have a sense of him just enjoying  being able to do this based on the shots  of his face while he's watching this is  juxtaposed with another birthing scene  gone wrong Lena's Midwife informs Damon  that there's nothing more he can do his  wife's baby won't come he's given the  same opportunity to try the emergency  C-section that viserys had with Emma but  after he finds out she won't survive but  before he gives an answer Lena gets up  and leaves the room to take things into  her own hands she commands her Dragon to  end the pain that she's experiencing and  after some tense moments vegar  eventually does that as Damon looks on  Harwin and Lionel also experience a fire  fiery death laris's tongueless assassin  set a fire in Heron Hall while they're  asleep and that does them in both of  these are heart-wrenching in their own  way and both have huge implications  Damon and Rainier are both lost an  important person in their life viserys  is once again without a hand and it  turns out that Laris is way more crazy  than you might have guessed and doesn't  personally draw the line at kinslaying  rhaenyra also decides to move her family  to Dragonstone and gives lane or  permission to bring his Paramore along  for the ride we see them arrive we see a  quiet moment with viserys in his  Chambers kissing Amy's ring and then we  see Laris tell the queen that he took  the idea of getting her father  reinstated and ran with it I think she's  legitimately surprised that he went as  far as killing his family if anything I  think she was hoping he would do  something that would expose the  parentage of raniera's kids but she did  put it out there that she wanted  something thing to happen and you gotta  love how Laris turned that into a  situation where he made himself  indispensable I think in an episode that  really leaned into her negative traits  were supposed to interpret this last bit  as her not being so far gone and that  she wouldn't expect him to go to these  lanes and it makes for a satisfying  place to end the episode  so yeah I think they mostly pulled off  this big time Jump we missed a lot but  that's how the book is too and so it's  keeping with the spirit of things at the  same time we're getting a clearer  understanding of how a lot of these  things played out and much more  characterization in some cases A decade  is a long time you kind of really hear  that when Lenor talks about doing his  duty and keeping up his end of the  bargain for 10 years families have been  built time has passed but we had enough  of it when they were younger to be able  to follow their progression based on  looking at his head and I couldn't tell  for sure but it looks like viserys's  left arm is completely gone at this  point I would say that his condition is  continuing to get worse but again 10  years is a long time and it didn't  necessarily feel like he would have been  guaranteed to last that long at the end  of episode 5. I know he looks terrible  but has he gotten progressively worse or  did things start to improve after after  Orwell took over as Grand maester it's  hard to say but I guess we can suppose  that mellos died off screen in between  episodes it's not just you every single  character is less sympathetic than they  were the last time we saw them every  living character I guess since all the  ones we lost in this episode were pretty  great they just cleared the board of  people who seem to have their hearts  firmly in the right place in a just  World Lena and the strongs would have  survived the sympathy deficit is a bit  more noticeable with Allison and Kristen  but there are enough bad decisions being  made to go around the kids mostly seem  sympathetic at this point so I would say  just hold on to that while you can  because this is a generational story and  they're all coming up in the same system  that produce their parents and  grandparents and take a close look at  what people are doing because even the  ones that think they're righteous are  way more looking after their own  interests rather than trying to remake  that system I was a little hard on  Rainier earlier and I guess I should  clarify that she is just playing the  hand she was dealt it wouldn't have been  her first choice to marry a gay man in a  situation where she's expected to  reproduce and ensure her own line of  succession that was something that she  had to go along with to hold on to power  that she hasn't yet realized having  passed her children in her position is  still a big risk though and we gotta  look at some of the immediate effects of  that when Jace asked his mother if  Harwin was his father but this is  something that makes her flawed rather  than something that makes her evil I  think some of the discussion I see  around this comes from the Viewpoint  that the rest to Allison's children is  something that Otto cooked up on his own  but you can't forget that rainy saw the  problems of rhaenyra being the heir for  different reasons as did Lionel strong  he could put a lot of the blame on  viserys for not reworking the system to  ensure that she could actually rule  rather than just naming her Heir you  could put blame on Allison for not  accepting her offer to Mary Jace and  Helena and generally undermining her at  court this could have been a solution  that could have helped things but it  doesn't mean you should just let her off  the hook for all the decisions she makes  either viserys's inaction is consistent  with his characterization Allison's  being protective of her children in a  situation where she thinks she's been  pulled into this family where everyone  is against her is consistent with hers  and Ranier is thinking she should be  able to do whatever she wants because  she was born a Targaryen princess is  consistent with hers this episode made  me think about a quote from George R.R  Martin I read in one of the first  articles that came out about the show  where he's talking about the story being  like a Shakespearean tragedy he told the  interviewer there's no Arya a character  everybody's going to love they're all  flawed they're all human they do good  things they do bad things they're driven  by lust for power jealousy Old Wounds  just like human beings just like I wrote  them and what what I liked about this  episode is that we've arrived at the  point where it's clear that none of  these characters are of the type you can  root for you can choose sides and people  will but none of the main characters are  without things that you'll have to  overlook to do that for me it doesn't  really matter if I like them or where  they land on the Imagine scale of  morality as long as what they're doing  makes sense for the characters they've  been presented as and now that we've  reached this point things can really  take off and I think that's a great  place to leave things let me know in the  comments what you thought about this  episode and where things will go if you  haven't read the book and if you have  what did you think about the way things  are playing out they definitely move  some things around the timeline here and  it feels like a choice not to spend too  much time on Harwin and Lena so if you  want to talk book spoilers that's fine  just please add a couple line breaks put  them below the fold so that people won't  see them unless they want to please like  this video If you enjoyed it please  subscribe to my channel if you haven't  already and thanks for watching I'll  talk to you soon
 

